Hello everybody,

Maybe it is a silly question, but I'd loke to confirm one of the parameters obtained via getAssociationWithTSS.

Does a negative value of dist.to <http://dist.to> feature  mean that the methylation is located before the TSS?

 Example taken from the table shown in this post.

      target.row dist.to.feature feature.name <http://feature.name> feature.strand

 331            5         -125403    NR_038008              +

*In this case, looking at the value -125403, does it mean that the TSS is 125403 before the TSS?

Thanks in advance for your answer.

JL

~#~####################################################

El viernes, 9 de agosto de 2013, 21:28:57 (UTC+2), sumithr...@gmail.com escribió:
> Hi , I did getAssociationWithTSS on an annotated object and I got the following which looks like
>
>       target.row dist.to.feature feature.name <http://feature.name> feature.strand
> 322            1          359267    NM_172851              +
> 1119           2          247261    NR_102306              +
> 19             3          513215 NM_001160370              +
> 330            4            4615 NM_001012322              +
> 331            5         -125403    NR_038008              +
> 331.1          6          -87672    NR_038008              +
>
>
> What is in the first column (322, 1119 etc)? Is this an identifier for the original differentially methylated base?
>
> Thanks--Sumithra
>
>

