Hello everybody,

I'm afraid that I need further explanation in this topic too.

Does the comparison depends on the values given for the "set of conditions" (sample.ids: test1 test2 ctrl1 ctrl2) & (treament: 1 1 0 0 ) or on the order.
I mean, if the "conditions" order is changed (sample.ids: ctrl1 ctrl2 test1 test2 ) &(treament: 0 0 1 1  );
Would we still get the same values? or changing the order of the conditions would change the direction of the comparative also?

Thanks in advance for your reply

JL

El miércoles, 15 de enero de 2014, 8:31:26 (UTC+1), Ngoc Tu Le escribió:
> Hi guys,
> I would like to ask about how to interpret the result given by calculateDiffMeth function in methylKit package. For example, if the sample.id <http://sample.id> is input with the order ("test","control"), then DMRs are derived by applying differential test in which order: control vs. test or test vs.control? This piece of information is important yet I could not figure out from the accompanying description.
> Thanks much in advance.
> Best,
>
>
>

From ue4181d5c40fc094c at groups.google.com  Mon Jul 13 15:29:42 2015
From: ue4181d5c40fc094c at groups.google.com (Kalyan K Pasumarthy)
